From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 05:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: adaptive prompt-cache admission -- the cache pays to
 fill itself and its hit rate is exactly zero (+0.3% score on top of 0059)

The same defect as 0059, one layer up. `get_available_slot()` runs
`prompt_save()` on every slot reuse -- a full `llama_state_seq_get_data_ext` of
the sequence state, 73 MiB on this model plus whatever context-checkpoint
payloads 0054 moves in with it -- and then immediately calls `prompt_load()`,
which searches the cache for an entry sharing a prefix.

**Censused with `llama-server --verbosity 4` over a replica session: the
`found better prompt` count is 0.** Every request logs

```
srv load:  - looking for better prompt, base f_keep = 0.000, f_sim = 0.000
srv load:    - prompt with length 541, lcp = 0, f_keep = 0.000, f_sim = 0.000
srv get_availabl: prompt cache update took 7.79 ms
```

The ranked harness gives every request a unique prefix
(`Sources/runner/base.ts`), so `lcp` is 0 or 11 out of 534 and no entry is ever
selected. The store is pure loss, at 7.8-10.4 ms and 73+ MiB per request.

`admit()` makes the store self-tuning: it is suspended after a run of misses,
any hit refills the credit in full, and a probe entry is admitted every 64 tasks
so a workload that starts sharing prefixes recovers on its own. **The LOAD path
is untouched** -- entries already held stay searchable, and a slot's own prompt
continuity does not go through this cache at all.
`LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_PROMPT_CACHE=0` restores stock behaviour and is the A/B toggle.

**Timing.** Same binary, env toggle, 8 arms interleaved
ctl/ck/pc/both/both/pc/ck/ctl x 9 measured runs, cache-cold replica of
`Sources/runner/base.ts`:

| arm | TTFT | prefill tok/s | decode tok/s | minflt/ttft req | AnonHugePages |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| ctl | 0.16037 | 5350.6 | 161.47 | 891 | 5033984 kB |
| pc  | 0.15456 | 5236.2 | 161.44 | 485 | 126976 kB |
| pc  | 0.15477 | 5299.9 | 160.96 | 485 | 126976 kB |
| ctl | 0.16251 | 5230.7 | 161.01 | 840 | 5185536 kB |

Alone: **ttft 0.16144 -> 0.15466 (x1.0438), prefill x0.9957, decode x0.9998**,
a = 6.8 ms / b = 7.1 ms / c = 6.6 ms, ranked-priced **+0.45%**. The retained
huge-page state going 5.03 GB -> 0.12 GB is the mechanism measured without a
clock.

**On top of 0059 it is worth +0.29%, not +0.45%**, and that is the honest
figure to carry: with checkpoint creation already suppressed the cache entry is
73 MiB rather than 199 MiB, so there is less left to skip. The `both` arm reads
ttft 0.13091, prefill 5469.8, decode 161.16 -> a = 30.5 / b = 27.7 / c = 30.1 ms
-> **+2.67% ranked-priced for the pair**, against +2.37% for 0059 alone.
Cross-checked against the zero-rebuild `--cache-ram 0` probe on the frontier
binary (ttft 0.16155 -> 0.15455), which the adaptive form matches.

**Correctness: this one is exactly bit-identical on the served path.** Unlike
0059 it moves no batch boundary -- it only skips a state copy nobody reads.
16 varied prompts x 64 greedy tokens through `llama-server`, both arms, same
binary: **16/16 byte-identical, max |dlogprob| = 0.000e+00.**

The gate binary is the same file as the parent commit's
(`libggml-hip.so.0`, `libllama.so.0`, `llama-perplexity`,
`libllama-common.so.0.0.10276` all md5-identical); only
`libllama-server-impl.so` changes, and `llama-perplexity` does not load it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
index 3f12834cc..cbf2ee707 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -1716,7 +1716,11 @@ private:
 
                 // [TAG_PROMPT_SAVE_CONSUME] on this path the slot prompt is dead on
                 // return: prompt_load() either overwrites it wholesale or we clear it.
-                ret->prompt_save(*prompt_cache, /* consume */ true);
+                // [gainz] adaptive admission: skip the state copy while this cache
+                // is not producing hits.  The load below is unaffected.
+                if (prompt_cache->admit()) {
+                    ret->prompt_save(*prompt_cache, /* consume */ true);
+                }
 
                 if (!ret->prompt_load(*prompt_cache, task.tokens)) {
                     ret->prompt_clear();
diff --git a/tools/server/server-task.cpp b/tools/server/server-task.cpp
index d26bbef80..cff2f8527 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-task.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-task.cpp
@@ -1810,6 +1810,9 @@ bool server_prompt_cache::load(server_prompt & prompt, const server_tokens & tok
         prompt = std::move(it_best->prompt);
 
         states.erase(it_best);
+
+        // [gainz] this cache just paid for itself -- see admit()
+        last_hit = true;
     }
 
     return true;
diff --git a/tools/server/server-task.h b/tools/server/server-task.h
index 9c542b5bc..23c5b27ba 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-task.h
+++ b/tools/server/server-task.h
@@ -653,6 +653,54 @@ struct server_prompt_cache {
     // moved into the cache entry instead of deep-copied.
     server_prompt_cache_state * alloc(server_prompt & prompt, size_t state_size_main, size_t state_size_drft, bool consume);
 
+    // [gainz] adaptive admission.
+    //
+    // Filling this cache costs a full llama_state_seq_get_data_ext of the
+    // sequence state on every slot reuse -- 73 MiB on this model, plus whatever
+    // context-checkpoint payloads come with it -- all of it first-touch host
+    // memory.  It only pays for itself if a later request finds a cached entry
+    // that shares enough of a prefix (`load()` picking an `it_best`).  On traffic
+    // where prompts do not overlap the hit rate is exactly zero and the fill cost
+    // is pure loss.
+    //
+    // A cache with a zero hit rate should stop paying to fill itself: `admit()`
+    // suspends the store after a run of misses, any hit restores it in full, and
+    // a probe entry is admitted periodically so a workload that starts sharing
+    // prefixes recovers on its own.  The LOAD path is untouched -- entries
+    // already held stay searchable, and prompt continuity within one slot does
+    // not go through this cache at all.
+    bool adaptive = [] {
+        const char * e = getenv("LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_PROMPT_CACHE");
+        return e == nullptr || atoi(e) != 0;
+    }();
+    int  credit   = 2;
+    int  idle     = 0;
+    bool last_hit = false;
+
+    static const int CREDIT_MAX  = 4;
+    static const int PROBE_EVERY = 64;
+
+    bool admit() {
+        if (!adaptive) {
+            return true;
+        }
+
+        if (last_hit) {
+            credit   = CREDIT_MAX;
+            idle     = 0;
+            last_hit = false;
+        } else if (credit > 0) {
+            credit--;
+        }
+
+        if (credit == 0 && ++idle >= PROBE_EVERY) {
+            credit = 1;
+            idle   = 0;
+        }
+
+        return credit > 0;
+    }
+
     bool load(server_prompt & prompt, const server_tokens & tokens_new, llama_context * ctx_tgt, llama_context * ctx_dft, int32_t id_slot);
 
     void update();
-- 
